  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> a balanced starting point is <strong>1.6&ndash;2.2&nbsp;g of protein per kg</strong> of body weight, <strong>25&ndash;35% of calories from fat</strong>, and the rest from carbohydrate. Calories come from your maintenance needs, minus 15&ndash;20% to lose fat or plus about 10% to gain muscle.</p></div>

